# The desktop comes up on a bare codex-vm -gop guest and paints its chrome:
# the top bar and its clock, the sidebar buttons, the Shutdown button and
# the Welcome window with its text wrapped (fester, main 12350).
#
# The clock is frozen. The taskbar paints the CMOS RTC, which is host state
# the test cannot twist, and that is what -rtc exists for -- without it this
# frame differs from the recorded one by the digits every single run.
#
# PARKED 2026-08-03 (Damian): while GopDesk is under active development this
# golden is NOT to be re-minted as routine and no new pane goldens are to be
# added. "They will change for silly reasons and it becomes ceremony not
# certainty." Nothing runs codex/test/gui/ automatically, so this costs no
# gate; the frame below is kept as the record. docs/ExaminersAssay.md, "PARKED
# during active GUI development", has the reasoning and what resumes it.
#
# Re-minted 2026-08-03 (red) when the Welcome hint gained "Monitor (m) reads
# the machine." The diff was 3752 pixels in a bounding box of x 418..949,
# y 480..531 -- the second and third hint lines and nothing else. The window
# did NOT move: both the old and new hint wrap to three lines at 42 columns
# (94 and 125 characters), so dk-win-h is unchanged, and a re-mint that had
# shifted the panel would have differed across every row of it instead.
#
# The font row is load-bearing and it reads "CBF bitmap (no TTF on the ESP)":
# no disk is attached, so desk-font's fallback is what is under test here as
# much as the chrome is. A run that ever painted the TTF face would mean the
# harness had grown a medium and this frame no longer says what it says.
vmargs -gop-width 1280 -gop-height 800 -rtc 2026-07-30T06:00:00
boot 4000
settle 2500
